      "fish_size_unit": "The early WRAM trials recorded raw stored size before its displayed unit was traced. Later ROM evidence confirms the selected size is copied into the keepnet unchanged and displayed in centimetres.",
      "later_rom_size_unit_clarification": {
        "rom_sha1": "c2103dd94e2a1a65a495fc02adc2e7d040f31212",
        "claim": "The live fish size is copied unchanged into the landed-fish state and keepnet record; the keepnet renderer formats that value as centimetres. Food ID 08 reads that same stored keepnet size, divides by four with integer truncation, and substitutes 1 when the result is zero. The formula is established by the ROM handler; the runtime species/size samples above remain the historical controlled observations.",
